# ~/.config/zsh/dircolors — LS_COLORS source, Nord palette (matches your fzf colours).
# Read by 05-lib.zsh via `dircolors -b`; the result is cached and regenerated
# automatically whenever this file changes. Used by ls, eza, zsh completion, fzf-tab.
#
# No TERM lines on purpose: every entry is global, so the cached output is valid for
# every terminal (alacritty, tmux, linux console ...).
#
# Format:  <type or .ext>  <SGR codes>      38;5;N = 256-colour foreground, 01 = bold
# Nord 256-colour approximations:
#   frost  109 teal   110 blue    67 dark blue
#   aurora 131 red    173 orange  222 yellow   108 green   139 purple
#   snow   188 / 255      polar night 59 (dim grey)

RESET 0

